    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0421" n="411" xml:id="pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/606: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-11T23:00:00+01:00">March 11, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 11—6:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2014. We hear that the Foreign Office, Beaverbrook’s office and the Air Ministry
                    are incensed by the articles said to have appeared in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aviation Daily</hi> during the last few days publishing
                    British and United States aviation agenda and promising to publish the Canadian
                    agenda, et cetera. Reference Embassy’s telegrams 1823, March 6, 7 p.m. and 1857,
                    March 7, 8 p.m.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d323-f1"/> and also first paragraph top of
                    page 2 of Satterthwaite’s letter to Walstrom of February 22.<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d323-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Will you please cable me the facts in regard to the alleged publication.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d323-f1" n="54" xml:id="d323-f1-content">
